# Solar PV System Analysis Calculator - Implementation Plan

## Goal Description
Create a comprehensive web application that analyzes the uploaded solar PV system report image, identifies all calculation parameters, and builds a tool allowing users to input parameters and generate professional reports matching the reference format. The application will feature a premium UI with calculation engine, data visualizations, and PDF export capability.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Based on the uploaded image analysis, the report appears to be a **PVGIS (Photovoltaic Geographical Information System) analysis report** containing:
> - Project metadata (location, system specs, orientation)
> - Solar radiation and performance data tables
> - Scatter plots for correlation analysis
> - Polar sun path diagrams (yellow shaded areas)
> - Monthly energy production bar charts (red bars)
> - Statistical summaries
> 
> Please confirm if this matches your requirements or if you need specific calculations/sections prioritized.

## Proposed Changes

### Application Structure

The application will be a single-page web application with the following components:

#### [NEW] [index.html](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/solar-pv-calculator/index.html)
Main HTML structure containing:
- Input form section for all solar PV parameters
- Live calculation display area
- Report generation and preview section
- Export to PDF functionality

#### [NEW] [styles.css](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/solar-pv-calculator/styles.css)
Premium design system featuring:
- Modern color palette with gradients (blues/oranges for solar theme)
- Glassmorphism effects for cards/inputs
- Smooth animations and transitions
- Responsive grid layouts
- Professional report styling matching the reference image

#### [NEW] [app.js](file:///C:/Users/samsung/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/solar-pv-calculator/app.js)
Core application logic including:
- Input parameter management
- Solar PV calculation engine (irradiance, energy yield, performance ratio, etc.)
- Dynamic chart generation using Chart.js
- Polar diagram visualization
- Report generation and formatting
- PDF export using jsPDF

---

### Key Features

**Input Parameters (Based on Report Analysis)**:
- **Location Data**: Latitude, Longitude, Elevation, Time zone
- **System Configuration**: 
  - PV module type and rating (kWp)
  - System losses (%)
  - Array orientation (azimuth, tilt angle)
  - Mounting type (fixed, tracking)
- **Database Selection**: Climate/irradiation database choice
- **Time Period**: Start/end dates for analysis

**Calculations**:
- Monthly solar irradiation (kWh/m²)
- Monthly energy production (kWh)
- Performance ratio (PR)
- Temperature effects
- System efficiency
- Annual totals and averages

**Visualizations**:
- Scatter plots (irradiation vs production correlation)
- Polar sun path diagrams with shading analysis
- Monthly bar charts (production/irradiation)
- Summary tables with statistics

**Report Sections** (matching uploaded image):
1. Header with project info and logo area
2. Input parameters summary table
3. Monthly performance data grid
4. Scatter plot analysis
5. Sun path polar diagrams (dual views)
6. Monthly production bar charts
7. Statistical summary table

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Load the application in browser using `browser_subagent`
- Test input validation for all parameter fields
- Verify calculations produce reasonable results
- Confirm all charts render correctly
- Test PDF export functionality

### Manual Verification
- Review the generated report against the uploaded reference image
- Verify aesthetic quality matches modern premium standards
- Ensure responsive design works on different screen sizes
